\section{Experiments}
\label{sec:methodology}
This section presents the methodology to answer the main research question, namely what is the effect of unannounced incoming flights on the performance of the system using different resource allocation strategies. In Section \ref{ss:meth_experiments} the test cases will be explained. Afterwards, in Section \ref{ss:property_change}, the implementation of the test cases in the model is elaborated.


\subsection{Experiments: strategies and scenarios}
\label{ss:meth_experiments}
In a situation after a natural disaster event most scheduled flights fly if possible. However, extra flights come in and their arrival is not always announced. According to experts, this causes a disruption in the planning \cite{weeks}. 
An overview of all test cases in this research are summarised in Table \ref{tab:experiments}. 
