The framework follows the methods outlined in \cite{Hsiao2021MAVFIAE},  utilizing a YAML file-based error configuration system to define the fault space. The configuration parameters include fault injected topic type (lidar or camera sensor), ROS message type, input and output topics, error type (``corrupted", ``drop", or ``delay"), error value (magnitude), and error frequency. This configuration approach enables systematic and reproducible fault injection across various components of the ROS2 system.

