The PointGAT method (+PointNet) is based on PointNet to achieve 3D embeddings but does not account for the impact of rotational invariance. This means that the same input may lead to unstable outputs due to the randomness of the initial state. 
Our proposed method enhances rotational invariance by calculating the expectation under SO(3). The average and maximum results from multiple experiments are shown in Table \ref{tab:ri}, demonstrating that our method produces more stable outputs.



