Fig.~\ref{fig:pio_vs_k} shows the overall performance of our method with different sample values $k$. It can be observed that when $k$ increases, the MAE for most properties initially decreases significantly and then starts to fluctuate. This indicates that more sampling angles provide more comprehensive geometric feature information, which helps enhance overall prediction performance. However, as the $k$ value continues to grow (e.g., $k=32$, $k=64$, $k=128$), most metrics begin to fluctuate around lower MAE values, demonstrating that most parameters do not require larger $k$ values.
