\section{Analysis of the object recorded by the Ukrainian armed forces in the combat zone}

Source of nighttime UAP observations: Instagram account \cite{Inst}. The date of the video upload is 24-2-2024. Video title: "Exclusive footage sent in by a military unit. The 406th battalion of the UAF captured some kind of UAP on its drone while observing the front line".

Later (27-2-2024), the British newspaper Daily Mail wrote about the sighting, also referring to the 406th Battalion video, under the headline "Ukrainian Armed Forces record UFO in a combat zone. EXCLUSIVE: Disk-shaped UFO filmed by Ukrainian military in combat zone."

The video was taken from a DJI Mavic 3T drone with a thermographic camera. The characteristics are given in \cite{Mavik}.

DJI Mavic 3T specifications: (1) sensor - uncooled Vox microbolometer, (2) 12 $\mu$m pixel, (3) 30 Hz frame rate, (4) MP4 video format, (5) infrared wavelength 8 to 14 $\mu$m.

The video is 17 seconds long. A typical frame of the video is shown in Fig. 9.

