			\begin{lemma}
				If the segment $I$ is not dense, then $\mathcal{SSI}(I) \preceq \mathcal{SAI}(I)$.
				\begin{proof}
					Consider the set $\mathcal{M}$ of points $p$ such that $p \in I, |A(p)| < \frac{99}{100}$. $\frac{|I|}{100} \ge A_0(I) \ge \frac{99}{100}(1 - |\mathcal{M}|)$, hence $|\mathcal{M}| \ge \frac{98|I|}{99}$.

