\n{\it Remark --}
The statistical test studied in this note is distribution-free, as is the WMW test;
that is, the distribution of the statistic $V$ does not depend on the continuous distribution under
$H_0$ of the random variables $X_t$ forming the time series.
To illustrate this fact, one can, after using the standard normal distribution,
estimate the distribution of $V$ by simulating, for example, \lstinline|Nsim=10^5| i.i.d. samples of the uniform distribution over the interval $(0,1)$, and then compare the two resulting empirical distributions.

\blst
set.seed=123
Nsim=10^5 
X = matrix(runif(n * Nsim), nrow = Nsim, ncol = n)  # Nsim white noise as rows 
clust=makeCluster(nclust)
