\section{The motive of the cone}\label{gojpergewrfwefwf}


Recall the universal coarse homology theory  $\Yo$ from \eqref{gjiwejrgoewrijogwerf}.
If $X$ is a bornological coarse space with a big family $\cY$, then we set
$$\Yo(\cY):=\colim_{Y\in \cY} \Yo(Y)\ , \quad  \Yo(X,\cY):=\Cofib(\Yo(\cY)\to \Yo(X))\ .$$

Let $X$ be in $\UBC$.
The generating members $ \Sq_{\le n}(X)$ of the big family $\Sq_{-}(X) $  are preserved by the $\nat_{-}$-action by down-shifts.
We therefore get an $\nat_{-}$-action on $\Yo(\Sq(X),\Sq_{-}(X))$ in $\CM$.
Since all elements of $\nat_{-}$ act by equivalences it extends to a $\Z$-action.
We indicate the twist of this action by  the sign character $\sign:\Z\to \{\pm 1\}$
by a superscript $\sign$.
Implicitly we use here  the existence of a corresponding functor $\sign:B\Z\to B\{\pm 1\} \to B\Aut_{\Sp}(S)$.
