 We let $[p]$ denote the image of $p$ in the relative coarse $K$-homology group $$\pi_{0}K\cX(\Sq(X)//G,\Sq_{-}(X)//G)\ .$$ 
Since $[p]$ is $\Z$-invariant, the class 
 $(\pm 1)[p]$ (see \cref{kopggwregweg} for notation)  is annihilated by $1+t$ in the fibre sequence  \eqref{rewgerfewrfwe}. By this fibre sequence, copying the ideas from \cite[Sec. (4.2)]{Kitsios:2025aa},
