As displayed in Figure \ref{fig::unweight-unif-c}, all three methods control the FDR across different values of $t$.
The conservativeness of {\tt cmc} aligns with our observation for weighted networks.
While the FDR of {\tt dss} exceeds that of {\tt clp}, its relative low power can be attributed to the heterogeneous missing probabilities. In general, both {\tt clp} and {\tt dss} outperform {\tt cmc} in the unweighted network setting, and our method demonstrates strong performance across both weighted and unweighted networks.




